<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Coronea (447 BC)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">447 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Battle of Coronea (447 BCE) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-peloponnesian-war">First Peloponnesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Coronea of 447 BCE was fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>, where Boeotian exiles and their allies defeated an Athenian force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tolmides">Tolmides</a> as it withdrew. The Athenian defeat ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>' control of Boeotia, won after Oenophyta in 457 BCE, and allowed the Boeotian League to re-form under Theban leadership. It was a turning point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-peloponnesian-war">First Peloponnesian War</a>.</p></div>
